The system tvm_ffi's ~ObjectDef() registers a ShallowCopy function whose lambda
takes a raw `const Class*` argument.  Function::FromTyped() needs
TypeTraits<const Class*>::TypeStr() to generate the signature string, but the
system headers only specialise TypeTraits for ObjectRef (not raw pointer) types.
Deleting the copy constructor makes std::is_copy_constructible_v<Class> false so
the `if constexpr` branch is never instantiated.

